5) Common gotchas (and fixes)
	•	Margins: always fit on pseudo-obs (ranks). Don’t assume Normal/t margins unless you checked.
	•	Near-collinearity: if PC1 ~ ΔlogS nearly linear, residualize PCs on ΔlogS first; then fit the vine on [PCres…, ΔlogS].
	•	Over-Gaussian: if the fit picks Gaussian everywhere, restrict family_set to {student, clayton, gumbel} initially to force tail-aware families; then re-open the set.
	•	Negative dependence: you need rotations=True so the library uses rotated Clayton/Gumbel to capture lower/upper tails with negative signs.

⸻

6) If you prefer a single (non-vine) copula

pyvinecopulib is for vines. For a single t-copula in d-D, use statsmodels’ StudentTCopula on pseudo-obs. It gives closed-form tail-dependence λ and is simpler, but cannot do asymmetric tails; use a vine when asymmetry matters.

